Atlas overlay patch 0073: ui/accent-seed
Why: the settings portal names the accent as the nearest of nine presets (violet comes out as purple), so the pill, ring and tab colours would show a colour near the person's accent, not it. The GTK theme WolOS-<id> states the exact accent (the selected-row background that kColorAccent already reads) and changes with the theme id, so the engine takes the theme's accent as the colour it seeds the palette with and the portal preset only when the theme states none. Lower tiers were not enough: the portal cannot carry an arbitrary colour (its accent-color is a preset), and a launcher flag (--disable-features=UsePortalAccentColor) removes the user_color seed of the sys palette altogether.
Files: ui/gtk/atlas_accent.h, ui/gtk/atlas_accent.cc, ui/gtk/atlas_accent_unittest.cc (new), ui/gtk/os_settings_provider_gtk.cc, ui/gtk/gtk_ui.cc, ui/gtk/BUILD.gn
Test filter: gtk_unittests --gtest_filter='*AtlasAccent*'; journey atlas-theme (reel R03)
Rebase risk: L (two one-line hooks in os_settings_provider_gtk.cc and gtk_ui.cc, two list lines in BUILD.gn; the logic is in new files)
Release: 0.13
License: GPL-3.0-or-later (hunks in files the inherited series touches or adds), BSD-3-Clause (new files)
